course: dictionary
lesson: 11334
title: Young and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word young has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Most often it means not old: «a young girl» is a girl who has lived only a short time.
explain: «When I was young» means at an early time in your life. The words «when I was» tell you the time is long ago, so young is about age.
explain: In a science text, «care for their young» means look after their babies. Here young is a noun, a thing rather than a describing word, and the clue is the caring. Ask yourself: is young describing someone, or standing for the babies?
fact: Young means having lived only a short time; it is the opposite of old.
fact: Young can mean at an early stage, just begun: «The night is young» means it is still early in the night.
fact: As a noun, the young are the babies of animals: «care for their young».
fact: «Younger» means a smaller age: «Tom is 3 years younger than Sam» means subtract 3 from Sam's age.
fact: «Young people» and «the youngest child» are common phrases that use young in everyday life.
exercise: «A young girl ran across the field.» What does young mean here? | Lost | Very tired | Very loud | *Not old
exercise: «The night is young.» What does young mean here? | *Just begun, still early | Lost | Very old | Tired
exercise: Sam is 9. Tom is 3 years younger than Sam. How old is Tom? | 4 | 3 | *6 | 12
test: «A child may not remember a parent who died when they were very young.» What does young mean here? | Sleepy | Happy | *Only a short time alive | Very old
test: Ana says, «The youngest child got the biggest slice.» What does youngest mean? | Oldest | *Smallest age | Tallest | Hungriest
exam: Read «young Portly hasn't learnt to swim very well yet.» What does young mean here? | *Not old, a young animal | Brave | Old | Wealthy
